If `just ckeletin-update` stops and the uncommitted path is `.ckeletin/cache/`, that directory is a retired update-check stamp from framework 0.2.30. It is not one of your changes. Delete it and run the update again.

rm -rf .ckeletin/cache
just ckeletin-update

If you updated from framework 0.2.30, that command re-resolved the whole Cargo.lock. The 0.2.30 command cannot print this note. After that update, restore the lock and refresh only the framework crate:

git checkout HEAD -- Cargo.lock
cargo update -p ckeletin

Framework 0.2.35 added `LogConfig.file_best_effort`. If you construct `LogConfig` in code, set the field. `false` keeps the previous behavior: `init` returns the error when the audit file cannot be opened. `true` warns once on stderr and the command continues.

The failure report added in 0.2.36 (the compiler or test diagnostic in `CKELETIN_UPDATE_RESULT`, and the handoff to `ckeletin-update-continue`) runs on updates that start from 0.2.36. The update that installs 0.2.36 still uses the recipe you already have. This note is what that update can show before it compiles.

Framework 0.2.37 checks a public crate's dev-dependencies and build-dependencies, including the same tables under `[target]`. A `package = "domain"` rename counts as domain. `[allowlists] public` is still only the normal dependencies. If the cli crate has no library, remove `public_imports_cli` and do not compile_fail it. Copy that file only when a declared cli package has a `[lib]` target or `src/lib.rs`.
